ment via the underlying throttler instance.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which throttler state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available throttler state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been completed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastExecutionTime"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamp of the last execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nextExecutionTime"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamp of the next allowed execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThrottlerOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Setter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ThrottledSignal.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThrottledSignal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const throttledScrollY = injectThrottledSignal(0, { wait: 100 })\n\n// Get value\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY())\n\n// Set/update value (throttled)\nthrottledScrollY.set(window.scrollY)\n\n// Access throttler\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY.throttler.state().isPending)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"value","text":"value","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectThrottledSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\nselector?): ThrottledSignal<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/injectThrottledSignal.ts:63](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/throttler/injectThrottledSignal.ts#L63)\n\nAn Angular function that creates a throttled state signal, combining Angular's signal with throttling functionality.\nThis function provides both the current throttled value and methods to update it.\n\nThe state value is updated at most once within the specified wait time.\nThis is useful for handling frequent state updates that should be rate-limited, like scroll positions\nor mouse movements.\n\nThe function returns a callable object:\n- `throttled()`: Get the current throttled value\n- `throttled.set(...)`: Set or update the throttled value (throttled via maybeExecute)\n- `throttled.throttler`: The throttler instance with additional control methods and state signals\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying throttler instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which throttler state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable throttler state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the last execution\n- `nextExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the next allowed execution\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<`ThrottlerOptions`\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ThrottledSignal`](../interfaces/ThrottledSignal.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst throttledScrollY = injectThrottledSignal(0, { wait: 100 })\n\n// Get value\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY())\n\n// Set/update value (throttled)\nthrottledScrollY.set(window.scrollY)\n\n// Access throttler\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY.throttler.state().isPending)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectThrottledSignal\ntitle: injectThrottledSignal\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectThrottledSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\nselector?): ThrottledSignal<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [throttler/injectThrottledSignal.ts:63](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/throttler/injectThrottledSignal.ts#L63)\n\nAn Angular function that creates a throttled state signal, combining Angular's signal with throttling functionality.\nThis function provides both the current throttled value and methods to update it.\n\nThe state value is updated at most once within the specified wait time.\nThis is useful for handling frequent state updates that should be rate-limited, like scroll positions\nor mouse movements.\n\nThe function returns a callable object:\n- `throttled()`: Get the current throttled value\n- `throttled.set(...)`: Set or update the throttled value (throttled via maybeExecute)\n- `throttled.throttler`: The throttler instance with additional control methods and state signals\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying throttler instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which throttler state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable throttler state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the throttler is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the last execution\n- `nextExecutionTime`: Timestamp of the next allowed execution\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<`ThrottlerOptions`\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ThrottledSignal`](../interfaces/ThrottledSignal.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst throttledScrollY = injectThrottledSignal(0, { wait: 100 })\n\n// Get value\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY())\n\n// Set/update value (throttled)\nthrottledScrollY.set(window.scrollY)\n\n// Access throttler\nconsole.log(throttledScrollY.throttler.state().isPending)\n```\n"}
